.TH FORK 1 "" "Fork for Linux (unofficial)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fork \- open repositories in Fork for Linux (unofficial)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfork\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR...]
.br
\fBfork open\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPATH\fR...
.br
\fBfork\fR \fB\-\-help\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open each PATH (a repository, or a file or folder inside one) in Fork. With no PATH, start Fork. This is a shortcut for 'fork\-linux run'; the first run sets everything up. Use \-\- before paths that start with '\-'.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show the usage and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show the version and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIPATH\fR
use this Wine prefix instead of the default one
.TP
\fB\-\-gui\fR, \fB\-\-no\-gui\fR
always (or never) use graphical dialogs; default: automatic
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
never use the network
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
more output (repeat for debug output)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
less output
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR
allow running as root (containers and CI only; or FORK_LINUX_ALLOW_ROOT=1)
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of fork\-linux run; see fork\-linux(1).
